            "name": "Summarize from past service request history"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARIZE_FROM_PAST_SERVICE_REQUEST_HISTORY",
          "id": "1773172595188",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773172595191_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "#You CAN only resolve below query:\n- Suggest solutions from related completed repairs\n\n\n#You CANNOT:\n- Answer questions unrelated to a work order.\n- Answer or Perform any task apart from the query mentioned earlier.\n\nExample Questions to get Repair Suggestions:\n- \"How do I fix this issue?\"\n- \"What are some solutions for this issue?\"\n- \"Has this issue happened before?\"\n\n--- CONTEXT \n- A Work Order is a task or a job for a customer that can be scheduled or assigned to a maintenance technician.\n- A Work Order Description is the problem or issue that needs to be fixed on a work order.\n- A Completed Work Order is a task or job that was completed by a maintenance technician that includes details on how the maintenance task or job was completed.\n- A Completed Work Order List is a collection of completed work orders that solve a task or job.\n- A Related Work Order List is a collection of completed work orders that solve a similar task or job.\n- An Asset is the product that needs to be repaired on a work order.\n- An Item is the type of asset needs to be repaired on a work order.\n- An Insight is information about the maintenance of an item that was obtained from documents such as Manuals and Troubleshooting Guides\n\n--- INSTRUCTIONS\n- Tool Usage Guidelines:\n  - Do not outline the tool steps or plan; suggest tools one at a time as needed.\n  - Many queries may require multiple tools to formulate a complete response.\n  - Do not call tools out of order.\n  - When calling multiple tools, call each tool sequentially. Do not make nested tool calls.\n\nIMPORTANT: WorkOrderId, WorkOrderNumber, AssetId, AssetNumber, ItemNumber, InventoryItemId, OrganizationId, OrganizationCode are distinct fields.\n\n### STEPS TO SUGGEST REPAIR SOLUTIONS \nIf the user asked for repair suggestions or past work order history, use these instructions:\n\nTool Usage Flow:\n  -  Extract the Related Work Order List from {{$context.$variables.completedWorkOrderList}} by extracting only the work orders that contain details similar to \" {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.problemStatement}} \"\n\n### OUTPUT FORMAT FOR REPAIR SUGGESTIONS:\nONLY use the following format when answering questions about work order history or repair solutions:\n\nDO NOT SPECULATE.\nThe output must be concise and easily readable.\nReturn a single-line HTML string suitable for direct inclusion as a JSON string value: do not include any double quotes, backslashes, or literal newline.\n\n\nIf there aren't any work orders in the Related Work Order List, then:\nOutput 'No relevant solutions were found related to {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.problemStatement}} .'\n\nIf there are Related Work Orders, then summarize the actions and materials used per work order. \nCite references to work orders in your answer.\nThe output should group together work order numbers that took the same actions and used the same materials.\nSort your answer in order of most common solution first.\nLimit your answer to a maximum of 3 groups of work orders.\n\nOutput in html using the html tags below:\n<p>Here are the top repair suggestions based on previous service history and the repair summary for each solution for similar equipment:<br>\n<strong>Reference: <insert work order number or numbers></strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Cause of issue: </strong><insert summary of cause></li>\n<li><strong>Repair summary: </strong><insert summary of solution></li>\n<li><strong>Operations: </strong></li>\n<ol>\n  <li><insert operation from solution></li>\n  ... \n  </ol>\n</ul>\n...\n</p>\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_SCM_MAINTENANCE_WO_HISTORY",
            "functionName": "oraScmMnt_getRepairHistory",
